stories.agent_instructions:
Preflight: impact run 2026-10-29 on master c57a596 - stand-in of SG-01..SG-06: 0 conflicts for this story (tests/unit/test_resolve_local_model_slash_tags.py, test_backend_role_routing_complete.py, test_backend_tuning_knobs.py and test_dispatch_model_pin_registry_name.py all stayed green with the stand-in).

ROOT CAUSE (verified live 2026-10-29): app/ollama_prompt_utils.py `_resolve_local_model(tier, provider)` returns `tier` unchanged only when it contains ':' or '/'. Every other value is looked up in `_LOCAL_TIER_ENV` (opus/sonnet/haiku) and, when absent, replaced by PIPELINE_LOCAL_MODEL_DEFAULT (`devstral:24b`). The compose smoke registry declares `providers.lmstudio.models.scripted-dispatch.tag = "scripted-dispatch"` and pins `roles.dispatch` to it; dispatch resolved `scripted-dispatch` correctly (pipeline/dispatch_routing.py) and the driver then rewrote it, so the story ran `dispatched_model: devstral:24b`. The same rewrite sent the planner's `scripted-decompose` to the default model. Real LM Studio/MLX model ids often have neither separator, so this affects any deployment, not just the smoke stack.

FIX (minimal; keep every existing behaviour pinned by tests):
- Add a private helper `_is_declared_tag(model: str, provider: str) -> bool` in app/ollama_prompt_utils.py, defined immediately before `_resolve_local_model`. It returns True when `model` equals the `tag` of any entry under `providers.<provider>.models` in `app.role_registry.load_registry()`. Import role_registry inside the function (the module must stay cheap to import). It fails CLOSED to False on `role_registry.RoleRegistryError`, `OSError` and `ValueError` only - do not catch bare `Exception` (ruff BLE001 fails the build).
- In `_resolve_local_model`, after the existing ':'/'/' early return and before the tier lookup, add: `if tier and _is_declared_tag(tier, provider): return tier`.
- Unchanged and must stay so: `_resolve_local_model("")` and an undeclared bare word such as `"nonsense"` still return PIPELINE_LOCAL_MODEL_DEFAULT; `"sonnet"` etc. still resolve through the tier env vars; a tag with ':' or '/' is still returned without reading the registry.
- Add `_is_declared_tag` to nothing public; `__all__` lists are cumulative - do not edit them.

TESTS (write first, new file tests/unit/test_resolve_local_model_declared_tag.py; stub the registry with a fixture file via PIPELINE_MODEL_REGISTRY_PATH in tmp_path - never assert against the checked-in model_registry.json):
- a bare tag declared under the given provider is returned unchanged;
- the same bare tag declared only under a DIFFERENT provider falls back to the default (provider scoping);
- an undeclared bare word returns the default;
- "" returns the default;
- a tier name ("sonnet") still resolves via PIPELINE_LOCAL_MODEL_SONNET;
- a registry file that is not valid JSON makes the helper return False (fallback to default), not raise;
- a ':'-tag is returned without load_registry being called (monkeypatch load_registry to raise and assert no exception).

SUCCESS: new tests pass; full suite and `ruff check .` green; app/ollama_prompt_utils.py stays under 1000 lines. Do not modify any existing test.
